{title: New Every Morning}
{subtitle: Lamentations 3:22–23; Psalms 36:6; 2 Timothy 2:13; Exodus 16:14–35; Luke 22:54–62; John 21:15–17}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 82}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Eb] | [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Out in the [Bb]desert every morning there was [Eb]bread upon the ground
[Gm]Thin and flaky, fine as frost, and [F]not a soul went without
[Eb]Even when they grumbled and they turned [Bb/D]their hearts around
[Cm]Every single morning there was [F]manna to be found
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]The LORD's acts of mer[Eb]cy never cease
[Gm]His compassions never [F]come to an end
They [Bb]are new every morning
[Eb]Great is your faithfulness
[Gm]LORD, your mercy reaches to the heav[F]ens
[Eb]Your faithful[F]ness to the [Bb]clouds [Eb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]Peter swore he'd never leave him, but he [Eb]warmed his hands that night
By [Gm]a fire in the courtyard he denied [F]him three times
[Eb]Then beside the lake one morning, in [Bb/D]the early light so pale
[Cm]Three times he asked him, Do you love [F]me, and his mercy did not [Bb]fail
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
The LORD's acts of mer[Eb]cy never cease
[Gm]His compassions never [F]come to an end
They [Bb]are new every morning
[Eb]Great is your faithfulness
[Gm]LORD, your mercy reaches to the heav[F]ens
[Eb]Your faithful[F]ness to the [Bb]clouds
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Eb]If we are faithless, [Gm]he remains faithful
[Bb]For he cannot de[F]ny himself
[Eb]If we are faithless, [Gm]he remains faithful
[Bb]For he cannot deny [F]himself
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
They [Bb]are new every morning [Eb]
[Gm]Great is your faithful[F]ness
{end_of_verse}
